    {
      "Seq": 22,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 6,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 1824,
      "Actor": "Nyccolhoth Lhavyniwyn",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I find myself at dawn in the heart of the village, scenting the earth beneath my hooves and the tension in the air. My posture is wary, as if sensing an unseen threat, but I know this place from the warning in a peat cut\u0027s cracked surface. I catch the scent of earth and the posture of a well-drawn breath. Here, the stone rim warns with a silent kinship, as if the square holds a deep breath, and this well is its watchful eye.",
      "Written": "",
